const quickstartMdx = `---
title: Quickstart
description: Authenticate with an API key, create a project with the Acme Projects API, and add your first task to it from the command line.
---

Every request needs an API key, sent in the \`Authorization\` header as a bearer
token. Set it in your shell first:

\`\`\`bash
export ACME_API_KEY="your-api-key"
\`\`\`

## Create a project

Send a name to [Create a project](/api/projects/create-project):

\`\`\`bash
curl https://api.acme.example/v1/projects \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACME_API_KEY" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{"name":"Website relaunch"}'
\`\`\`

The response is the project, with the ID the API assigned:

\`\`\`json
{
  "id": 1,
  "name": "Website relaunch",
  "description": null,
  "created_at": "2026-01-15T09:30:00.000Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-15T09:30:00.000Z"
}
\`\`\`

## Add a task

Pass the project's ID to [Create a task](/api/tasks/create-task):

\`\`\`bash
curl https://api.acme.example/v1/projects/1/tasks \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACME_API_KEY" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{"title":"Write the launch post","due_on":"2026-02-02"}'
\`\`\`

## Handle errors

A request with a missing or unknown key gets a \`401\` with an \`error\` message.
An invalid body gets a \`422\`, with each invalid field listed under \`errors\`:

\`\`\`json
{ "errors": { "name": ["can't be blank"] } }
\`\`\``;

